{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_lease", "label": "Lease interface", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "The framework's distributed-lock abstraction: implementations differ in backing store, the contract does not.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_acquire", "label": "Lease.acquire", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "false means another holder definitively has it; a rejection means 'I do not know'. It is idempotent when this caller already holds the lease.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_acquirewithtoken", "label": "Lease.acquireWithToken", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "An optional variant returning a backend-issued fencing token; because it is optional, consumers feature-detect it and fall back to plain acquire.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_fencing_token", "label": "Fencing token", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Lets an external observer order two acquires against the same lease; backed by the coordination service's own optimistic-concurrency primitive (K8s resourceVersion, Redis SETNX with a counter, etcd revision) and compared as an opaque exact string.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_release", "label": "Lease.release", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A no-op when not held, but it rejects when the backend could not be told \u2014 the record stays claimed on the server while the process dropped it locally, and that is worth knowing. It also does nothing while an acquire is still in flight, because ownership only begins when that acquire resolves.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_checkalive", "label": "Lease.checkAlive", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A synchronous local check with no roundtrip, so it reflects up to one missed renewal of staleness \u2014 use it to gate work, not as proof of ownership.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_onlost", "label": "Lease.onLost", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Fires once per unexpected loss; the handler must drop ownership state immediately without awaiting expensive work, because another holder may already be acting.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_etcdlease", "label": "EtcdLease (custom backend sketch)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_custom_backend_requirements", "label": "Three requirements for a custom backend", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Atomicity on acquire from the backend's own consistency model, periodic renewal at roughly ttl/3, and onLost accuracy including the TTL-expiry case.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_leasemajority", "label": "LeaseMajority (lease consumer)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The one caller that acts on a release rejection: it enters fail-safe and stops claiming majority until the partition heals. It also feature-detects acquireWithToken.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_ttl_pause_hazard", "label": "A TTL cannot tell a crash from a pause", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A GC stall or suspended VM longer than the TTL silently loses the lease, so the TTL must exceed the worst-case pause.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_lease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_acquire", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_lease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_acquirewithtoken", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/coordination/lease-api.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_lease", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_coordination_lease_api_release", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0